","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dcf215b1814c49dd8e4a56e7a6f27c52c2eda4b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/dcf215b1814c49dd8e4a56e7a6f27c52c2eda4b9","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/dcf215b1814c49dd8e4a56e7a6f27c52c2eda4b9"}]},{"sha":"f19f9f7abd692f9ca624e1632674bf92834c29b5","node_id":"C_kwDOPUU0qdoAKGYxOWY5ZjdhYmQ2OTJmOWNhNjI0ZTE2MzI2NzRiZjkyODM0YzI5YjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-06T22:43:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-06T22:43:44Z"},"message":"docs(ci-cd): principle 10 — a serialised writer still starts behind\n\nThe concurrency group decides the order in which main-writing jobs run; it\ndoes not re-point their working trees. `actions/checkout` checks out\n`github.sha`, so the second writer in the queue begins one or more commits\nbehind the branch it is about to push to, and its push is rejected as\nnon-fast-forward. Following principle 10 exactly therefore turned \"two\nwriters collide\" into \"the second writer reliably fails\" -- deterministic and\nloud, and still a broken release (link-foundation/browser-commander: the Rust\ncrate reached 0.10.11 on crates.io while `Cargo.toml` on `main` said 0.9.0;\nthe Python package was never published at all).\n\nPrinciple 10 now states the gap, rules out `ref: main` on the checkout and\nsays why (it builds, tests and publishes a tree CI never validated, with\nnothing in the log to say so), and prescribes the recovery: classify the\nrejection first, because a GH006/GH013 ruleset rejection prints `rejected`\ntoo and can never be satisfied by a rebase, then rebase and retry. Four\nfurther rules cover the ways the retry itself goes wrong: `--force-with-lease`\non a shared branch, a version recomputed from the stale tip, success reported\nbefore the push landed, and an unbounded retry loop. Principle 9 gained the\nmatching bullet for the pull-request recovery, so the cross-reference holds\nin both directions. Added to all four translations.\n\ntests/cicd-best-practices-serialised-writers-2220.test.mjs pins the parts\nthat must not be translated and checks that this repository still implements\nthe recovery it now documents (scripts/version-and-commit.lib.mjs).\nexperiments/issue-2220-serialised-writer-race.mjs reproduces the whole thing\nwith local git: two writers that never overlap, the rejection, and the same\npush landing on the second attempt with the first writer's commit intact.\n\nIssue #2220","tree":{"sha":"429db7077ed956d537b3208430c0edd3efb46367","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees/429db7077ed956d537b3208430c0edd3efb46367"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits/f19f9f7abd692f9ca624e1632674bf92834c29b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/f19f9f7abd692f9ca624e1632674bf92834c29b5","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/f19f9f7abd692f9ca624e1632674bf92834c29b5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/f19f9f7abd692f9ca624e1632674bf92834c29b5/comments","author":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff3e44579876b16393c2038f8182472db81bf99c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/ff3e44579876b16393c2038f8182472db81bf99c","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/ff3e44579876b16393c2038f8182472db81bf99c"}]},{"sha":"d91baa1d336839102a1caa7a8ac1b38f70d7679f","node_id":"C_kwDOPUU0qdoAKGQ5MWJhYTFkMzM2ODM5MTAyYTFjYWE3YThhYzFiMzhmNzBkNzY3OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-06T21:25:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-06T21:25:07Z"},"message":"docs(ci-cd): add principle 16, \"Prove You Can Publish Before You Build\"\n\nAdded to all four language versions of the guide, after \"15. Audit the\nDependency Tree\", with the evidence behind each bullet: why a login is\nnot a probe (ghcr.io hands a push-scoped token to any credential it\naccepts; docker.io answers an anonymous push-scope request with 200 and\na pull-only access claim), why the preflight must report every failure\ninstead of the first, why reachability is a separate question from\nwritability, why trusted publishing beats a credential with an expiry\ndate, and why `unknown` must never be rounded to either answer.\n\ntests/cicd-best-practices-publish-preflight-2221.test.mjs keeps the four\ncopies in step on the parts that must not be translated -- the HTTP verbs,\nthe workflow keys, the gating expression -- and checks that release.yml\nactually follows the principle the guide states.\n\nIssue #2221","tree":{"sha":"00ff3cc55b2b02cbfda2c1a7ed59305e4fc422e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees/00ff3cc55b2b02cbfda2c1a7ed59305e4fc422e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits/d91baa1d336839102a1caa7a8ac1b38f70d7679f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/d91baa1d336839102a1caa7a8ac1b38f70d7679f","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/d91baa1d336839102a1caa7a8ac1b38f70d7679f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/d91baa1d336839102a1caa7a8ac1b38f70d7679f/comments","author":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"72d591149c2d2efbff9184fc5dbc8c8b9f1fb47b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits/72d591149c2d2efbff9184fc5dbc8c8b9f1fb47b","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/commit/72d591149c2d2efbff9184fc5dbc8c8b9f1fb47b"}]},{"sha":"a4bea2c66f617e36a0f4a510b7b4786c0fac9256","node_id":"C_kwDOPUU0qdoAKGE0YmVhMmM2NmY2MTdlMzZhMGY0YTUxMGI3YjQ3ODZjMGZhYzkyNTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T14:21:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"konard","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-04T14:21:31Z"},"message":"docs(2198): write the two gates this PR added into the best-practices guide\n\nThe issue asks that the work follow `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`. Two of\nthe findings are gates the guide never described, so following it could not\nhave prevented them -- both were absent here and are absent from the\ntemplates that guide points at.\n\n§14 \"Lint the Workflows Themselves\" records the actionlint + zizmor pairing\nand, above all, the trap that made this worth writing down: actionlint must\nrun as the Docker image, because a bare binary with no `shellcheck` on PATH\nskips every `run:` block and exits 0. That single detail was the difference\nbetween finding fourteen shell bugs in `release.yml` and finding none.\n\n§15 \"Audit the Dependency Tree\" records the hole between CodeQL and\nPR-scoped dependency review, and the three flags that decide whether the\njob means anything: `--package-lock-only`, an explicit `--audit-level`, and\na schedule trigger.\n\nBoth sections land in all four translations, as the existing guide tests\nrequire. `tests/cicd-best-practices-pipeline-gates-2198.test.mjs` pins them\nthe same way #2152 pins §13; it was 